Local test-only adjustment for deterministic Happy Eyeballs fallback.

Upstream report: https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/48767

The first four destinations must fail before the local IPv4 server is reached.
A public endpoint can report an early TCP connection on the randomly chosen port.
Use unbound loopback addresses and their IPv4-mapped IPv6 forms so the test keeps
its six-attempt ordering, response assertions, and original attempt timeout.

--- a/test/parallel/test-net-autoselectfamily.js
+++ b/test/parallel/test-net-autoselectfamily.js
@@ -70,8 +70,8 @@
       host: 'example.org',
       port: port,
       lookup: createMockedLookup(
-        '2606:4700::6810:85e5', '2606:4700::6810:84e5', '::1',
-        '104.20.22.46', '104.20.23.46', '127.0.0.1',
+        '::ffff:127.0.0.2', '::ffff:127.0.0.3', '::1',
+        '127.0.0.2', '127.0.0.3', '127.0.0.1',
       ),
       autoSelectFamily: true,
       autoSelectFamilyAttemptTimeout,
@@ -84,10 +84,10 @@
       assert.deepStrictEqual(
         connection.autoSelectFamilyAttemptedAddresses,
         [
-          `2606:4700::6810:85e5:${port}`,
-          `104.20.22.46:${port}`,
-          `2606:4700::6810:84e5:${port}`,
-          `104.20.23.46:${port}`,
+          `::ffff:127.0.0.2:${port}`,
+          `127.0.0.2:${port}`,
+          `::ffff:127.0.0.3:${port}`,
+          `127.0.0.3:${port}`,
           `::1:${port}`,
           `127.0.0.1:${port}`,
         ]
